            "finding": "A plan that just meets its proof misses the target: 12 requests a week over 16 days is about 27 quotes, about 8 wins, about $2,720 against $3,000; no rule for results between stop and proof.",
            "resolution": "Accepted, and the arithmetic checks out (12 x 16/7 = 27.4 quotes x 0.3 = 8.2 wins = $2,720). The proof is now 15 requests and 3 wins by day 7, and selling runs to day 22, with invoices on day 23 that settle on day 29, inside 30. At the proof rate that is about 49 quotes and 14 wins. The middle band (6-14 requests or 1-2 wins) extends the test to day 10, needing 21 requests and 5 wins, else stop."
